format deletes the definition. The output is just

    Just a paragraph.

and the URL, which appears nowhere else in the file, is gone for good.

What it should do: write the definition back out. A definition that no link
uses yet is still text the author wrote, and the next edit is likely to use
it.

Cause: cmark-gfm consumes a link reference definition while parsing and stores
it in the document's reference map rather than leaving a node in the tree, so
MarkdownParser.parse never sees one and FormatCommand has nothing to write.
Keeping it needs the definitions read out of the source text before the tree
is walked, since the parser will not hand them back.

Related, and owned by another case: a definition that IS used survives only as
the inline URL pasted into the link that referenced it.
